      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "The closest analogue, differing only by replacement of the morpholine oxygen with a silamorpholine unit, showed a mouse oral B/P AUC0-inf ratio of 1.69 and was explicitly labeled as good penetration, directly supporting meaningful CNS access for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "A closely related oxazolidinone with the same N-aryl scaffold and a dithiocarbamate side chain exhibited a B/P AUC0-inf ratio of 3.49 in mice, demonstrating robust brain penetration for this chemotype.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C14"],
      "claim": "A difluorinated analogue of the same oxazolidinone series showed a B/P AUC0-inf ratio of 2.65 in mice, confirming that additional polarity/fluorination on this scaffold still permits good brain penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "High-similarity oxazolidinone analogues with the same acetamidomethyl side chain and N-aryl substituent show B/P AUC ratios of 1.69–3.49 in mice, indicating meaningful CNS access; the query's morpholine variant is expected to retain adequate brain penetration.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental measurement for the exact morpholine-containing query molecule.",
    "B/P ratios are total brain-to-plasma ratios, not unbound brain concentrations, so efflux or binding differences cannot be fully excluded.",
    "Silamorpholine analogues are slightly more lipophilic than the morpholine query, which could modestly alter permeability or transporter recognition."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

